     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Two controls suffice: mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin. Phishing is always available, so the attacker always gets foothold_workstation and stolen_user. With no segmentation the attacker reaches the internal network. mfa_user is bypassed because the attacker holds foothold_workstation, so auth_appserver/apiserver/ciserver work. Kerberoasting then gives stolen_admin, and escalate_ciserver plus leak_secrets_ciserver give stolen_dbadmin. Every exfiltration path needs auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup. With mfa_dbadmin deployed, these need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which mfa_admin blocks. So exfiltration is impossible. (segmented plus patched:workstation and patched:laptop also blocks reach_internal, but that uses 3 controls.) No single control works. mfa_admin alone still allows stolen_dbadmin via ciserver, so auth_db succeeds. mfa_dbadmin alone is bypassed via admin_dc. segmented alone is bypassed by escalating on the phished workstation. mfa_user is bypassed by the phished footholds. Each patch leaves alternative paths open. So the minimum is 2.\"}"
    }
   ],
